+The verification checks row counts, quote accounting, promise ordering, and
+per-keyset liabilities. It does not re-hash the public keys the mint will serve.
+Start the mint and fetch `/v1/keys/{id}` for every advertised keyset, then
+recompute the NUT-02 id from the served keys and compare it with the advertised
+id. A truncated or incomplete amount list keeps every key correct but changes
+the hash.
+
+## Historical data
+
+The migrator reads common historical data tolerantly:
+
+- NULL quote states are treated as UNPAID.
+- NULL, empty, or literal `None` payment lookup ids fall back to the quote id.
+- int4 `amount`/`fee_reserve` columns are read through `::bigint` on PostgreSQL.
+- An empty keyset `amounts` list falls back to 64 denominations.
+- Melt-quote expiry beyond the int4 (2038) ceiling is clamped.
+
+Duplicate paid/pending melt quotes with a real payment id still abort. Resolve
+them on the source copy before migrating.
+
 ## After migration
 
 Initialize the database-backed configuration with the original seed:
